artifact.self_contained_problem:
A numerical semigroup is a subset $\Gamma \subseteq \mathbb{N} = \{0,1,2,\dots\}$ that is closed under addition, contains $0$, and has finite complement in $\mathbb{N}$. For such a $\Gamma$, define:

- the multiplicity $\operatorname{mult}(\Gamma)$ as the smallest positive element of $\Gamma$;
- the embedding dimension $\operatorname{edim}(\Gamma)$ as the cardinality of the (unique) minimal system of generators of $\Gamma$ as a semigroup;
- the set of pseudo-Frobenius numbers $\operatorname{PF}(\Gamma) = \{\, n \in \mathbb{Z}\setminus \Gamma : n + \gamma \in \Gamma \text{ for every } \gamma \in \Gamma \setminus \{0\}\,\}$;
- the type $t(\Gamma) = |\operatorname{PF}(\Gamma)|$.

For integers $e$ and $m$ with $3 \le e < m$, set
$$T(e,m) \;=\; \sup\{\, t(\Gamma) \;:\; \Gamma \text{ is a numerical semigroup with } \operatorname{edim}(\Gamma) = e+1 \text{ and } \operatorname{mult}(\Gamma) = m \,\}.$$

Determine $T(e,m)$ as an explicit function of $e$ and $m$.
